eferrer noopener\">SEO KPIs<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/ai-seo-tools\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">AI SEO Tools<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/search-engine-functions\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Search Engine Functions<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/best-website-speed-test-tools\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Website Speed Test Tools<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/seo-chrome-extensions\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Best SEO Chrome Extensions<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">11. Keyword Placement<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>While writing content, it is obvious that the keyword and related <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/lsi-keywords\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">LSI keywords<\/a> will occur naturally in the text body.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>However, there are a few places to place your target target keywords intentionally:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Page Title: <\/strong>The title of the page appears on the page.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Title Tag: <\/strong>This title of the page appears on the SERP.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>First 100 Words of the Page: <\/strong>Ensure that you incorporate this naturally.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Headings: <\/strong>Ideally in at least two H2s on the page.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Meta Description: <\/strong>Summary of the web page that appears on the SERP.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Image Alt Text: <\/strong>It is an image\u2019s text alternative.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Image File Name: <\/strong>Don\u2019t save an image as \u2018Screenshot-1\u2019 or \u2018chart.\u2019<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">12. Content Quality<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Always keep your audience in mind while creating your on-page SEO. Keywords help you rank higher in the SERPs; however, focus on producing quality and relevant content that will be helpful to your readers. For instance, if the readers search for \u201cWhat is on-page SEO?\u201d create an informative guide on the topic.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Some of the tips for writing quality content:<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Use the appropriate heading tags<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Provide accurate information<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Provide links to external sources when citing statistics and studies.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">13. Schema Markup<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Schema markup is a set of data that allows search engines to learn about your content better using post tags. The more Google knows about the type of your website and every content on it, the more efficient your overall on-page SEO will be. Google pulls more data from the posts with schema markup and displays rich snippets in its SERPs.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">14. Social Sharing<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Social sharing of your content using social sharing buttons on your blogs\/articles will boost your online presence, contributing to your SEO efforts.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">15. User Experience (UX)<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Google prioritizes the experience that users have with their products\/services. So, ensure that your UX is user-friendly. A good user experience improves your website navigation, lessens bounce rate, and boosts time on the page and engagement.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Ways to achieve a positive user experience:<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Optimize the website\u2019s design, layout, and readability&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Focus on mobile responsiveness, easy navigation, and clear CTAs<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Offer valuable, relevant content<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">16. Spelling And Grammar<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Although spelling and grammar are not the ranking factors, the user experience is. Content with multiple spelling and grammatical errors offers the worst user experience. This further discredits your content\u2019s authority and legitimacy. So, always focus on publishing error-free content.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also Read: <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/search-engine-functions\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Major Functions of Search Engine (How Search Engines Work)<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">17. E.E.A.T Signals<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>E-E-A-T, which stands for Experience, Expertise, Authoritativeness, and Trustworthiness, plays a crucial role in Google\u2019s ranking system. It is not an algorithm or ranking factor. E-E-A-T is not directly measurable. The raters use E-E-A-T as a guide and the ratings they report back to Google inform any future algorithm changes. E-E-A-T is more essential than the current ranking factors and algorithms since it signals the future of those factors and algorithms. E-E-A-T is future-proofing your online presence.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-d72f351059e80039135382f58233f821\"><strong>Explore Our Most Popular Marketing Courses<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/digital-marketing-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogTable&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Digital Marketing Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/performance-marketing-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogTable&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Performance Marketing Course<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/seo-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SEO Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/ai-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">AI Course<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">FAQs on On-page SEO Checklist<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"schema-faq wp-block-yoast-faq-block\"><div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1717063734078\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">1. <strong>What are the major elements of on-page SEO?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Key on-page SEO elements include optimizing title tags, meta descriptions, content (including keyword usage), internal links, URLs, and images and ensuring a positive user experience. These elements collectively contribute to improved search engine rankings and user engagement.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1717063751306\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">2. <strong>What is the difference between off-page SEO and on-page SEO?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Off-page SEO optimizes signals outside your website, such as building <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-are-backlinks\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">backlinks<\/a> and establishing a social media presence. On the other hand, on-page SEO involves optimizing elements directly on your web pages, like content, meta tags, and internal links.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1717063761515\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">3. <strong>How often should I perform on-page SEO?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">On-page SEO is more than just a one-and-done task. Regular monitoring and updates are essential, with a suggested frequency of at least once a month for routine checks. Conduct more in-depth assessments quarterly to ensure your content stays relevant and aligned with evolving search engine algorithms.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1717063784086\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">4. <strong>How vital is on-page SEO for overall website performance?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">On-page SEO is integral to overall website performance. It directly impacts search engine rankings, user experience, and content discoverability. Neglecting on-page SEO can hinder your site&#8217;s visibility and user engagement.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1717063790772\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">5. <strong>Explain the difference between on-page SEO and technical SEO.<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">On-page SEO optimizes individual web pages to boost search engine rankings and user experience. <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/technical-seo\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Technical SEO<\/a> is a portion of on-page SEO that optimizes the technical aspects of your entire website, ensuring it&#8217;s crawlable and indexable and performs well from a technical standpoint.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1717063844447\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">6. <strong>Name the tools available to assist with on-page SEO.<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Several tools aid in on-page SEO efforts. Tools like Semrush, Moz, and Ahrefs offer features for keyword research, content optimization, and performance tracking. Utilizing these tools can streamline the on-page optimization process and provide valuable insights for improvement.<\/p> <\/div> <\/div>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/seo-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=Content_Banner&amp;utm_campaign=SEO&amp;utm_page=on-page-seo-checklist\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1000\" height=\"210\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/07\/seo-course.webp\" alt=\"seo course\" class=\"wp-image-11966\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/07\/seo-course.webp 1000w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/07\/seo-course-300x63.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/07\/seo-course-768x161.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" \/><\/a><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Conclusion<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>We hope that this on-page SEO checklist will be a helpful resource for you as you optimize your web pages. Every SEO step and effort listed in this on-page SEO work list is directed toward success. As you optimize on-page elements, work on technical aspects, too, to yield the best results.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-e1fc883f2a064c2ee23f1a20caaaed0f\"><strong>Explore Our Free Courses<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/semrush\/free-course\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Semrush Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/google-tag-manager\/free-course\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">GTM Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"