, editorial best practices, and SEO principles to create high-quality, reader-focused resources that deliver value.","sameAs":["https:\/\/www.linkedin.com\/in\/ashimajain90\/"],"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/author\/ashima\/"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/on-page-seo-checklist\/#faq-question-1717063734078","position":1,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/on-page-seo-checklist\/#faq-question-1717063734078","name":"1. What are the major elements of on-page SEO?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Key on-page SEO elements include optimizing title tags, meta descriptions, content (including keyword usage), internal links, URLs, and images and ensuring a positive user experience. These elements collectively contribute to improved search engine rankings and user engagement.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/on-page-seo-checklist\/#faq-question-1717063751306","position":2,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/on-page-seo-checklist\/#faq-question-1717063751306","name":"2. What is the difference between off-page SEO and on-page SEO?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Off-page SEO optimizes signals outside your website, such as building <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-are-backlinks\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">backlinks<\/a> and establishing a social media presence. On the other hand, on-page SEO involves optimizing elements directly on your web pages, like content, meta tags, and internal links.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/on-page-seo-checklist\/#faq-question-1717063761515","position":3,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/on-page-seo-checklist\/#faq-question-1717063761515","name":"3. How often should I perform on-page SEO?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer